%N A400390 Irregular table read by rows: T(n, k) = gcd(d(n, k), n/d(n, k)), where d(n, k) = A027750(n, k) is the k-th divisor of n.
%H A400390 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400390/b400390.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10032</a> (rows 1..1360, flattened)
%F A400390 T(n, k) = T(n, tau(n) - k + 1), where tau(n) = A000005(n).
%F A400390 T(n, k) = 1 for all 1 <= k <= tau(n) if and only if n is squarefree (A005117).
%e A400390 Table begins:
